<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eudokia Dmitriyevna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1353–1407</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Evdokia Dmitriyevna, Euphrosyne of Moscow</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eudokia Dmitriyevna was Grand Princess of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> as the wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dmitry-donskoy">Dmitry Donskoy</a>, whom she married in 1366. A daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dmitry-of-suzdal">Dmitry Konstantinovich of Suzdal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizhny-novgorod">Nizhny Novgorod</a>, she sealed the alliance between the two princely houses. She founded the Ascension Convent in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow-kremlin">Moscow Kremlin</a>, became a nun under the name Euphrosyne shortly before her death in 1407, and is venerated as a saint.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eudokia-dmitriyevna.jpg" alt="Eudokia Dmitriyevna" width="320" height="367" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sergey Nikitin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eudoxia_of_moscow_reconstruction_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
